    summary: 'A stream is an in-order queue of work (kernels, copies, host callbacks) executed by the device in submission order; work in different streams may overlap. Events are markers recorded into a stream that other streams or the host can wait on, and that carry timestamps for measuring device-side time. PyTorch runs everything on the current stream of each device, which defaults to the legacy default stream, and uses side streams for copies, allocator-aware overlap and NCCL communication.',
