    memory: 'Workspace of hundreds of MB to GB per stream; fused epilogues save one read and write of the output per fused op.',
    knobs: ['Compute type and TF32 policy (torch.backends.cuda.matmul.allow_tf32)', 'cudnn.benchmark and deterministic flags', 'CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG', 'cublasLt epilogue fusion and FP8 scaling', 'Alignment and layout of operands (16-byte alignment enables the fast paths)', 'Custom CUTLASS kernels for quantized or grouped GEMMs'],
    metrics: ['Achieved TFLOP/s per GEMM vs peak (ncu, torch.profiler FLOP counts)', 'Which kernel was selected (kernel names in nsys, e.g. sm90_xmma, cutlass_*)', 'Fraction of step time in GEMM kernels', 'Workspace allocation size', 'Bit-exact reproducibility across runs when determinism is required'],
    failureModes: ['Heuristic choosing a poor kernel for odd shapes (padding to multiples of 8 or 16 often fixes it)', 'Misaligned or non-contiguous operands falling back to slow kernels', 'cudnn.benchmark re-searching on every new shape in a dynamic-shape workload', 'Non-deterministic results from split-K when reproducibility is expected', 'Workspace allocation failing under memory pressure', 'Library version changing kernel selection and perturbing accuracy or speed'],
